# PART I — HADES (2020)



## 1. Game overview

**Developer:** Supergiant Games  
**Original full release:** September 17, 2020  
**Genre:** Isometric action roguelike / roguelite  
**Perspective:** Fixed, elevated, isometric camera  
**Primary gameplay:** Real-time combat, dodging, ability combinations, dungeon exploration, character progression and repeated escape attempts.

Official game page: [Hades — Supergiant Games](https://www.supergiantgames.com/games/hades/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

### The premise

You play as Zagreus, the immortal Prince of the Underworld and son of Hades.

Zagreus wants to escape his father's realm and reach the surface. To do so, he must fight his way through increasingly dangerous regions of the Greek Underworld, face its guardians, receive assistance from the Olympian gods and discover why his family is so determined to keep him below.

The story features familiar mythological figures, including Hades, Persephone, Zeus, Athena, Poseidon, Artemis, Achilles, Nyx and Thanatos.

However, the game isn't simply a retelling of Greek mythology. It reimagines the gods as a dysfunctional family whose personal relationships, rivalries and secrets gradually emerge through dialogue.

The most important narrative decision is that **death is part of the story rather than a reason to restart it from scratch**. Each escape attempt, successful or otherwise, can advance conversations, relationships and character development. [Supergiant Games](https://www.supergiantgames.com/blog/hades-faq/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

### What type of game is it?

Hades is a roguelite.

That distinction matters because a typical run doesn't preserve every upgrade you collect. Instead, it combines temporary combat improvements with permanent progression that makes future attempts more manageable.

A run generally follows this pattern:

1. Choose a weapon and prepare at the House of Hades.
2. Enter a sequence of combat chambers.
3. Defeat enemies and choose rewards.
4. Build a combination of divine abilities.
5. Defeat a region's guardian.
6. Continue through increasingly challenging regions.
7. Escape, or die and return to the House.
8. Spend resources, unlock improvements, develop relationships and try again.

The precise sequence of chambers, rewards and available upgrades changes between runs. That variability is central to the game's replayability. [GameSpot](https://www.gamespot.com/reviews/hades-review-the-long-hard-road-out-of-hell/1900-6417568/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

