# 2. Hades: Combat mechanics in detail

Combat is the heart of Hades.

The game uses an elevated camera, relatively small arenas and highly responsive movement. You can see enemies surrounding Zagreus, anticipate attacks, reposition quickly and exploit openings.

The basic controls are simple. The depth comes from how you combine them.

## 2.1 The five fundamental combat actions

The core combat system revolves around five actions.

| Action | Function | Tactical purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Attack | Uses your weapon's standard attack | Consistent damage and combos |
| Special | Activates the weapon's secondary move | Alternate attacks, ranged damage or area control |
| Cast | Launches a magical projectile | Ranged damage, enemy marking and build synergies |
| Dash | Quickly moves Zagreus and can provide brief invulnerability during the movement | Avoiding attacks, repositioning and extending combos |
| Call | Uses a powerful divine ability after charging its gauge | Burst damage, temporary protection or other powerful effects |

Not every weapon uses these actions in the same way. Your chosen weapon determines the fundamental shape of your combat strategy.

The game also lets you combine movement with attacks, allowing you to evade an incoming strike and immediately counterattack rather than waiting through a separate defensive animation. [GameSpot](https://www.gamespot.com/reviews/hades-review-the-long-hard-road-out-of-hell/1900-6417568/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

### Why the dash is so important

Dodging isn't merely an emergency escape.

It is part of the offensive system.

For example, you might:

- Dash through an enemy's attack.
- Move behind the enemy.
- Use a rapid attack sequence.
- Activate your Special while the enemy recovers.
- Retreat before another enemy closes in.

This produces a continuous rhythm of movement, damage and evasion.

A player who attacks without paying attention to enemy animations can lose health quickly. A player who understands attack timing and positioning can make the same encounters look almost effortless.

**Design assessment:** Hades makes defence active. You don't stand still behind a shield waiting for an opening; you create your own opening through movement.

## 2.2 Attack patterns and combo flow

Each weapon has a distinct attack pattern, damage profile and range.

Some reward rapid, repeated hits. Others deal heavy damage through slower attacks or allow you to fight from a distance.

The game doesn't require complex fighting-game inputs. Instead, the challenge comes from choosing the right action at the right time.

A typical encounter involves four simultaneous decisions:

1. Which enemy should be attacked first?
2. Is it safe to remain in melee range?
3. Which ability or attack provides the best damage?
4. Where should Zagreus move before the next enemy attack?

As enemy density increases, these decisions become more important.

An attack that works against one isolated enemy might be a poor choice when surrounded by several enemies with different attack patterns.

## 2.3 The six Infernal Arms

Hades has six primary weapon families, known as the Infernal Arms. Each changes how you approach the entire run.



### A. Stygian Blade

**Combat identity: balanced melee combat.**

The Stygian Blade is the most straightforward starting point for understanding the game's combat.

Its attacks are built around close-range strikes, with a Special that can hit an area around Zagreus.

Strengths:
- A relatively intuitive attack pattern.
- Reliable damage at close range.
- Good opportunities to combine attacks and movement.
- A flexible foundation for different divine upgrades.

Weaknesses:
- You must approach enemies to deal much of your damage.
- Poor positioning can leave you surrounded.
- Some encounters are harder when enemies attack from several directions.

**Best suited to:** Players who enjoy direct melee combat and learning enemy patterns.

### B. Heart-Seeking Bow

**Combat identity: precision and ranged attacks.**

The bow lets Zagreus attack enemies from a distance. Its standard attack can be charged for a more powerful shot, while its Special releases multiple projectiles.

Strengths:
- Can damage enemies without remaining in melee range.
- Rewards careful positioning.
- Supports ranged builds and projectile-based strategies.
- Gives you more control over engagement distance.

Weaknesses:
- Charged attacks require timing.
- Firing opportunities can be interrupted by aggressive enemies.
- Positioning remains essential because ranged combat doesn't make Zagreus invulnerable.

**Best suited to:** Players who prefer precision, distance and controlled attacks.

### C. Shield of Chaos

**Combat identity: defence combined with flexible offence.**

The shield has a distinctive defensive capability and can also be used to attack enemies at a distance through its Special.

Strengths:
- Offers defensive options that other weapons lack.
- Can attack multiple enemies.
- Provides a different approach to managing dangerous encounters.
- Can support more forgiving playstyles.

Weaknesses:
- Its attack rhythm takes practice.
- Defensive positioning can become less effective if you fail to account for attacks from other directions.
- Its damage opportunities depend on the weapon configuration and upgrades.

**Best suited to:** Players who value defensive flexibility and want to control how enemies approach.

### D. Eternal Spear

**Combat identity: reach and flexible engagement distance.**

The spear provides a mixture of thrusting attacks, longer-reaching strikes and a Special that throws the weapon.

Strengths:
- More reach than close-range weapons.
- Can attack enemies at different distances.
- Offers a flexible balance between melee and ranged pressure.
- Supports several distinct upgrade strategies.

Weaknesses:
- Its attack timing can feel less immediate than faster melee weapons.
- Players must learn how to use its different moves effectively.
- Poorly timed throws or attacks can leave enemies free to retaliate.

**Best suited to:** Players who want flexible reach and varied attack options.

### E. Twin Fists of Malphon

**Combat identity: speed and close-range aggression.**

The Twin Fists specialise in rapid melee attacks.

Strengths:
- Fast attack sequences.
- Excellent potential for repeated-hit effects.
- A natural fit for aggressive, mobile play.
- Can feel extremely responsive once mastered.

Weaknesses:
- Requires close proximity to enemies.
- Makes positioning especially important.
- Can be punishing when an enemy's attack covers the area you're trying to occupy.

**Best suited to:** Players who enjoy fast movement, aggressive combat and repeated attacks.

### F. Adamant Rail

**Combat identity: ranged pressure and resource management.**

The Adamant Rail is a ranged weapon that uses ammunition for its standard attack. Its Special provides a separate area-damage option.

Strengths:
- Allows consistent ranged pressure.
- Offers a different combat rhythm from melee weapons.
- Can be combined with upgrades that enhance projectile damage.
- Supports builds focused on attacking multiple enemies.

Weaknesses:
- Its ammunition and reload rhythm must be managed.
- It can feel less intuitive to players accustomed to melee weapons.
- Effective damage depends on understanding when to attack and when to reposition.

**Best suited to:** Players who prefer ranged combat and enjoy managing attack cadence.

The important point is that these weapons aren't simply different skins. Their movesets affect positioning, attack timing, enemy selection and the kinds of divine upgrades that become most valuable. [teemo.dev](https://teemo.dev/game-design/hades/design/overview-notes/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

## 2.4 Weapon Aspects: customising the moveset

Each weapon has multiple Aspects that change its characteristics or mechanics.

This is important because unlocking a new Aspect can alter how a familiar weapon plays.

Instead of asking only, "Which weapon is strongest?", you start asking:

- Which version of this weapon fits my preferred strategy?
- Which upgrades complement its mechanics?
- Do I want to prioritise burst damage, repeated hits or utility?
- Which enemies will give this configuration the most trouble?

The result is a progression system in which learning a weapon doesn't mean you've exhausted its possibilities.

## 2.5 Boons: the game's central build system

Boons are temporary upgrades granted by the Olympian gods.

They can modify your attacks, Specials, Casts, dashes and other abilities.

Examples of the types of effects available include:

- Lightning effects that trigger additional damage.
- Water-based effects that provide knockback.
- Defensive effects that help mitigate incoming damage.
- Critical-hit effects that reward particular attack patterns.
- Damage-over-time or status effects.
- Improvements to your Cast or Call.
- Upgrades that make a particular ability substantially more effective.

The Olympians have different mechanical identities, so choosing a god can influence the direction of your entire build.



### How a build develops

Imagine that you choose the Heart-Seeking Bow.

During the first few chambers, you acquire an upgrade that improves your standard attack. Later, you find another boon that increases your damage against enemies affected by a particular status effect.

You then choose an additional upgrade that helps apply that effect consistently.

Your build now has a direction: attack from range, apply the effect and exploit the resulting damage bonus.

This is more interesting than simply collecting the upgrades with the highest individual numbers.

The value of an upgrade depends on what you already have.

### Rarity and synergy

Boons can differ in rarity, and some combinations are more powerful than others.

The system rewards players who understand relationships between effects.

For example, a defensive boon might seem less impressive than a damage upgrade. However, if it allows you to survive longer in a difficult boss fight, it can contribute more to a successful run.

Likewise, an upgrade that increases repeated-hit damage might be more useful with a rapid weapon than with a weapon that relies on occasional heavy strikes.

**Design assessment:** The boon system turns combat into a series of decisions rather than a fixed sequence of attacks. Every run gives you a different set of tools, and success depends partly on how well you combine them. [Supergiant Games](https://www.supergiantgames.com/blog/hades-faq/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

## 2.6 Daedalus Hammer upgrades

The Daedalus Hammer provides weapon-specific modifications.

Unlike a boon that adds a divine effect, a Hammer upgrade can change the weapon's behaviour more directly.

Depending on the weapon and available upgrade, this can mean changing an attack pattern, improving its reach or damage, or modifying a Special.

These upgrades can transform a weapon from a familiar tool into something that demands a different approach.

The distinction is useful:

- **Boons** build a broader combination of abilities and effects.
- **Hammer upgrades** modify the weapon itself.
- **Aspects** provide a more fundamental change to the weapon's identity.

Together, these systems create several layers of customisation without requiring the player to learn an entirely new control scheme for every build.

## 2.7 Casts and Calls

Two additional systems make the combat more varied.

### Cast

Your Cast provides a separate magical attack. Its effectiveness depends on your selected boons and the way you use it.

It can be useful when:
- An enemy is dangerous to approach.
- You need damage while repositioning.
- Your build contains effects that interact with Casts.
- You want another way to contribute damage between weapon attacks.

### Call

Your Call gauge fills during combat, allowing you to activate a powerful divine ability.

Calls can provide major offensive or defensive benefits, depending on the god associated with the ability.

The important decision is timing. Using a Call early can help clear a dangerous group, while saving it for a boss's vulnerable phase may provide more value.

These abilities encourage players to think about their entire toolkit instead of relying exclusively on the weapon's standard attack. [PlayStation](https://www.playstation.com/en-us/games/hades/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

