# 6. Hades II: Progression and customisation systems

Hades II retains the original's principle of persistent progression while expanding the number of systems through which Melinoë develops.

This makes the game more elaborate, but it also creates additional decisions for players to learn.

## 6.1 The Crossroads



The Crossroads is Melinoë's central hub between runs.

It serves a similar structural purpose to the House of Hades in the original.

Here, the player can interact with characters, prepare for another run, unlock upgrades and perform activities that contribute to long-term progression.

However, the Crossroads also supports a stronger sense of preparation and magical research.

It connects the game's combat systems to the wider theme of witchcraft.

## 6.2 The Altar of Ashes and Arcana Cards

The Altar of Ashes provides access to Arcana Cards, which grant persistent benefits.

These cards allow players to customise aspects of Melinoë's capabilities and influence how future runs develop.

The system encourages players to decide which advantages matter most to their preferred approach.

For example, one player might prioritise survivability, while another might invest in resources or combat effectiveness.

The important distinction is that the player isn't simply buying a single linear set of upgrades.

Instead, the system offers choices that influence the character's broader capabilities.

### Why this system matters

The Arcana system provides a more structured way to customise persistent progression.

It also introduces an additional strategic layer before the run begins.

Players must decide not only which weapon to use, but also which combination of persistent benefits will support their intended approach.

## 6.3 Incantations and crafting

Incantations allow Melinoë to perform magical rituals that unlock features, improve the hub or otherwise affect progression.

They connect the game's resource collection to its witchcraft theme.

Materials gathered during runs can contribute to longer-term objectives rather than serving only as immediate rewards.

This creates another reason to explore and collect resources, even when a particular item doesn't directly improve the current fight.

### Design trade-off

Additional progression systems create more opportunities for customisation.

However, they also increase complexity.

Players must learn what different resources do, which unlocks are worthwhile and how long-term improvements interact with the immediate demands of a run.

For players who enjoy experimentation, this can be rewarding. Players who prefer a more straightforward experience may need more time to become comfortable with the systems.

## 6.4 Gathering tools and reagents

Hades II introduces tools that help Melinoë gather resources during her journeys.

These tools connect exploration to crafting and long-term progression.

The player must consider which resources to pursue and how gathering opportunities fit into the current run.

This gives exploration a purpose beyond simply finding the next combat chamber.

## 6.5 Familiars

Melinoë can develop relationships with supernatural animal companions.

These familiars can provide useful benefits and contribute to the player's approach to a run.

Their role fits the sequel's emphasis on witchcraft and preparation.

They also add another progression dimension: players can invest in systems that support their journey beyond the weapon and Boon choices made during combat.

## 6.6 Keepsakes and relationships

Keepsakes return as a way to influence runs through character-related effects.

The game's expanded cast also creates additional opportunities for relationships and narrative progression.

Interactions with characters reveal more about their personalities, motivations and connections to the wider story.

As in the original, these systems make repeated attempts feel connected to an ongoing world rather than a sequence of disconnected combat challenges.

## 6.7 God Mode and escalating difficulty

Hades II includes God Mode, which provides a more forgiving experience for players who want to focus on exploration and story.

For players seeking greater difficulty, the game also includes escalating challenges through the Oath of the Unseen and related systems.

This gives players more control over the experience.

Someone learning the game can reduce the pressure of repeated encounters, while an experienced player can deliberately seek a more demanding challenge.

### Progression verdict

Hades II expands the original's progression system through Arcana Cards, Incantations, gathering tools, familiars and additional customisation.

These features make preparation more involved.

**The sequel gives players more ways to influence their runs, but it also asks them to understand more systems before they can make the most of that flexibility.** [Supergiant Games](https://www.supergiantgames.com/blog/hades2-faq/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

