# 7. Which game has better progression?

This is one of the clearest differences.

### Hades

The progression system centres on the Mirror of Night, weapon unlocks, Aspects, keepsakes, companions and relationship development.

The systems are interconnected, but their overall structure is relatively easy to understand.

You collect resources, unlock upgrades and return to the Underworld.

### Hades II

The sequel adds more systems to manage.

Arcana Cards, Incantations, gathering tools, familiars and additional unlocks expand the ways you can influence future runs.

This gives the player more opportunities to customise their experience, but it also increases the amount of information they must learn.

### Verdict

**Hades is more streamlined; Hades II is more elaborate.**

If you prefer a smaller number of interconnected systems, the original has a strong advantage.

If you enjoy collecting resources, unlocking new capabilities and experimenting with several progression systems, the sequel offers more to explore.

